<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Operation Polo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1948</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Police action in Hyderabad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Operation Polo was the Indian military operation of 13-18 September 1948 that ended the independence of Hyderabad State, whose Nizam had refused to join <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Officially termed a police action, it took place amid violence by the Razakar militia and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telangana">Telangana</a> peasant uprising. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad">Hyderabad</a>'s forces surrendered on 17 September, and the state was annexed to India.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/operation-polo.jpg" alt="Operation Polo" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Clarendon Press · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hyderabad_state_from_the_Imperial_Gazetteer_of_India,_1909.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
